# Line-ending normalization for reproducible content hashes.
#
# ragsec freezes and verifies approval over RAW FILE BYTES (pilot.compute_freeze: sha256_bytes of attack docs;
# experiments.dataset_content_hash: sha256 over dataset files). An LF<->CRLF conversion CHANGES those bytes and
# therefore the hashes, so it is NOT automatically harmless: on Windows a CRLF checkout would make a dataset's
# content_hash mismatch its manifest (load_dataset fails) and would register as freeze drift. These rules store
# and CHECK OUT text as LF on every platform so approval hashes are stable.
#
# NOTE: adding this file can trigger a one-time renormalization. Run `git add --renormalize .` deliberately (NOT
# done automatically here), review the diff, and re-generate/re-freeze any affected dataset so approved hashes
# match the normalized bytes. Never silently refresh an approved freeze to accommodate a line-ending change.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
